{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>See, he brought us a Hebrew man.</b> She did not specify who, and the intent is upon her husband. And that she did not mention him — this is the way of women's conduct. And that she said 'a Hebrew man' — he was regarded in the land, he and his fathers, as Hebrew men, after the name that they were from across the river. <b>To mock us.</b> As the language of the verse (Proverbs 10:23): ״כשחוק לכסיל עשות זמה״. <b>He came to me to lie with me.</b> She was full of wind: she had said to him 'lie with me,' yet she says 'he came to me to lie with me.'" "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> 'He came to me to lie with me' — this is what the verse says (Ecclesiastes 7): ״ומוצא אני מר ממות את האשה אשר היא מצודים וחרמים לבה אסורים ידיה״. Rabbi Yehudah bar Shalom says: there is nothing harsher than woman. Know that in the matter of the calf it is said (Exodus 32): ״ויפול מן העם ביום ההוא כשלשת אלפי איש״, and in the matter of Zimri, through a woman, fell (Numbers 25) twenty-four thousand. (Ecclesiastes 7): ״טוב לפני האלהים ימלט ממנה״ — this is Joseph. ״וחוטא ילכד בה״ — this is Zimri. What is ״אסורים ידיה״? They would seize a person in the marketplace. When the Holy One, blessed be He, created Eve, He said: From what place shall I create her? If from the head, her spirit would be haughty; if from the eye, she would be prying; if from the mouth, she would be a chatterbox; if from the ear, she would be an eavesdropper; if from the hands, she would be a thief; if from the feet, she would be a gadabout. What did the Holy One, blessed be He, do? He created her from the rib, which is a modest place, so that she would be modest and dwell in the house. And even though He did not create her from the head, her spirit is haughty, as it is said (Isaiah 3): ״יען כי גבהו בנות ציון ותלכנה נטויות גרון״. He did not create her from the eye, yet she is prying, as it is said (ibid.): ״ושקרות עינים״. And it is written (Genesis 3): ״ותרא האשה כי טוב העץ למאכל וכי תאוה הוא לעינים״. He did not create her from the mouth, yet she is a chatterbox, as it is said (Genesis 30): ״המעט קחתך את אישי״. He did not create her from the hands, yet she is a thief, as it is said (Genesis 31): ״ותגנוב רחל את התרפים״. He did not create her from the ear, yet she is an eavesdropper, as it is said (Genesis 18): ״ושרה שומעת פתח האהל״. He did not create her from the feet, yet she is a gadabout, as it is said (Genesis 30): ״ותצא לאה לקראתו״. (Genesis 34): ״ותצא דינה בת לאה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {1 "Isaiah 3:8 cited as 'ושקרות עינים' appears in some editions of Isaiah 3:16 (ושקרות עינים); the reference is approximate."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:01.808574308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}